 "source": "viem 2.55.4 alone, run under node 22.14.0: hashDomain (with getTypesForEIP712Domain), encodeType and hashStruct, hashTypedData, privateKeyToAccount(key).signTypedData, recoverTypedDataAddress (every signature recovers to its signer), parseSignature, keccak256, concat, toBytes, toHex, validateTypedData; walletJson is viem's own serializeTypedData({domain, message, primaryType, types: {EIP712Domain: getTypesForEIP712Domain({domain}), [primaryType]: fields}}), exactly what signTypedData hands a JSON-RPC account's eth_signTypedData_v4, with uint32 and uint64 fields given to viem as numbers (JSON numbers) and uint128, uint256 and uint256[] as bigints (decimal strings); intentId is keccak256(concat([intentIdTag, digest, signer address lowercase])) and signed is the relayer's payload, both mirroring exchange.papertrade.xyz's zy and Fy/Py/Ly functions (uint* and uint256[] as decimal strings, address and bytes* lowercase, bools as bools, v as \"27\"/\"28\", r and s lowercase 32-byte hex); the exchange and paperStaking separators were asserted against the contracts' on-chain DOMAIN_SEPARATOR() answers on 2026-10-13.",
